<title>FRANCE: Tietmeyer-EMU delay was not a topic at Lyon talks.</title>
<headline>Tietmeyer-EMU delay was not a topic at Lyon talks.</headline>
<dateline>LYON, France 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank president Hans Tietmeyer said that talks between German and French financial officials on Wednesday had not addressed the question of delaying the start of European monetary union.</p>
<p>Asked by reporters after the talks whether a delay in the launch of the single currency had played a part in the discussions he replied, &quot;Most definitely not.&quot;</p>
<p>Europe is due to create a single currency from 1999, but many would-be participants -- including Germany and France -- are facing problems meeting the criteria set for entry.</p>
</text>
